  "description": "NAJLUJ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H58 Eu4 N8 O36 Si8 2-,2(C24 H20 P1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.777-3.805 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.07-107.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (Ph4P)2[(PhSiO1.5)8(EuO1.5)4(O)(NO2.5)6(EtOH)2(MeCN)2].",
